meta {
  name: 19-Did my verification get approved?
  type: http
  seq: 19
}

get {
  url: {{host}}/api/notifications/mine?page=0&size=20
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{temi_token}}
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
}

docs {
  Since I can't query my verification status directly, I'm forced
  to check my notifications inbox to see if a VERIFICATION_APPROVED
  or VERIFICATION_REJECTED has arrived.

  Notification has a `payload` (typed as string but probably JSON)
  and a `kind` enum. As a UI consumer, I'd have to JSON.parse the
  payload string and switch on `kind` to format every line. That
  works. But the payload schema is opaque — the spec just says
  "payload: string" with no per-kind schema.
}
